-- The AHB side of the PBUF can store status for up to 3 pkt_done handshakes
-- from the MAC side of the PBUF -- once it gets to 3 status's held, it will
-- hold off the handshake back to the MAC side of the PBUF.  This will
-- cause the MAC to halt any more packet fetches as the 4th status cannot be
-- captured by the AHB.  The fetch of the 5th packet will therefore be 
-- delayed
--
-- In this test, we want the MAC side of the PBUF to send multiple (over 3)
-- pkt_complete handshake to the AHB side of the packet buffer before even
-- the first MANWR has been dealt with
-- This can be done by delaying the hready of the MANWR AHB access for ages
--
